{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nlong long powMod(long long x, long long y) {\n    long long ans = 1;\n    while (y) {\n        if (y & 1LL) ans = (ans * x) % MOD;\n        x = (x * x) % MOD;\n        y >>= 1LL;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int P, K;\n    scanf(\"%d%d\", &P, &K);\n\n    vector<int> parent(P, 0), rnk(P, 0);\n    for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n        parent[i] = i;\n        rnk[i] = 1;\n    }\n\n    auto find = [&](int x) {\n        while (parent[x] != x) {\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]];\n            x = parent[x];\n        }\n        return x;\n    };\n\n    auto unite = [&](int a, int b) {\n        if (rnk[a] >= rnk[b]) {\n            parent[b] = a;\n            ++rnk[a];\n        } else {\n            parent[a] = b;\n            ++rnk[b];\n        }\n    };\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n        int v = (int)((long long)K * i % P);\n        int a = find(i);\n        int b = find(v);\n        if (a != b)\n            unite(a, b);\n    }\n\n    vector<char> isRoot(P, 0);\n    int groupCount = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n        int r = find(i);\n        if (!isRoot[r]) {\n            isRoot[r] = 1;\n            ++groupCount;\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long ways;\n    if (K == 0)\n        ways = powMod(P, P - 1);\n    else if (K == 1)\n        ways = powMod(P, P);\n    else\n        ways = powMod(P, groupCount);\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", ways);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    static long powMod(long x, long y) {\n        long ans = 1;\n        while (y > 0) {\n            if ((y & 1L) == 1L) ans = (ans * x) % MOD;\n            x = (x * x) % MOD;\n            y >>= 1L;\n        }\n        return ans;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int P = sc.nextInt();\n        int K = sc.nextInt();\n\n        int[] parent = new int[P];\n        int[] rnk = new int[P];\n        for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n            parent[i] = i;\n            rnk[i] = 1;\n        }\n\n        java.util.function.IntUnaryOperator find = (int x) -> {\n            while (parent[x] != x) {\n                parent[x] = parent[parent[x]];\n                x = parent[x];\n            }\n            return x;\n        };\n\n        java.util.function.BiConsumer<Integer, Integer> unite = (Integer a, Integer b) -> {\n            if (rnk[a] >= rnk[b]) {\n                parent[b] = a;\n                ++rnk[a];\n            } else {\n                parent[a] = b;\n                ++rnk[b];\n            }\n        };\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n            int v = (int)((long)K * i % P);\n            int a = find.applyAsInt(i);\n            int b = find.applyAsInt(v);\n            if (a != b)\n                unite.accept(a, b);\n        }\n\n        boolean[] isRoot = new boolean[P];\n        int groupCount = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i < P; ++i) {\n            int r = find.applyAsInt(i);\n            if (!isRoot[r]) {\n                isRoot[r] = true;\n                ++groupCount;\n            }\n        }\n\n        long ways;\n        if (K == 0)\n            ways = powMod(P, P - 1);\n        else if (K == 1)\n            ways = powMod(P, P);\n        else\n            ways = powMod(P, groupCount);\n\n        System.out.println(ways);\n        sc.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0076298960484564304, -8.34461570775602e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -3.7788631743751466e-05, -2.5033637939486653e-05, 0.0, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -0.47950613498687744, -0.10022211074829102, -2.3245540432981215e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.015257081016898155, -0.0015036477707326412, -3.576214658096433e-05, -0.3134808838367462, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0007099968497641385, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0015029336791485548, 0.0, -0.001191144809126854, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -4.410734163684538e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.07888996601104736, 0.0, -9.703165414975956e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.12692835927009583, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.753696753643453e-05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.018149960786104202, 0.0, -0.3869107663631439, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.12972749769687653, -0.029750416055321693, -0.02990557812154293, 0.0, -6.198863957251888e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0